# Held latest native conversion-tool qualification route

This source-only successor copies the retained public native-host-tools harness.
It registers the portable upstream alias fixture on macOS using the production
reader, Windows writer and their actual helper closure. The complete relinker,
NID patcher and existing CTests remain registered through the supplied source.

Use the actual adopted private source and its frozen latest-plus20 source review.
Run receipt.py before and after; it compares every source hash and mode and all
11 initialized vendor commits/clean states directly against that review. The
optional adoption receipt is recorded by hash without inventing its outcome.

A fresh output directory must receive configure.log, build.log, ctest.log,
test-inventory.json, tests.xml, source-before.json and source-after.json. Use
Python3.12 and PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. Capture CTest --show-only=json-v1 and
run the complete inventory without a name filter. finalize.py takes the actual
--jobs value and the prior 110 test-inventory.json. Qualification requires the
actual configured names with all prior 110 and the required ca4 and 43b regressions, complete executed-name equality, no failed/skipped cases and
unchanged reviewed source/dependencies.

Compiler jobs are coordinated across native and Windows work: --parallel1 only
when Windows uses1 job, or --parallel2 only when Windows is joined. Configuration
can invoke compiler checks and follows the same coordination. Source preparation
alone is not a build, tool qualification, runtime/device or gameplay result.

The preserved targeted ARM64 baseline19 alias failure and patched20 success
are separate from the pending complete latest-case tool qualification.

The final upstream target for this cycle is 43bc17f7edfc32c38428fd8e4e6d8cc94c8cb31b. Source counts and extra current test names come from the frozen source review and actual configured inventory; earlier 114 is only the retained ca4 checkpoint.
